  "preamble": "The velar fricative [ɣ] shifts to the voiceless velar fricative [x] through devoicing. This process eliminates the voicing feature while preserving the place and manner of articulation, and occurs in various phonological contexts including word-final position and before voiceless consonants. In Akkadian, Proto-Semitic *ġ merged with the voiceless velar fricative ḫ [x] (*ṣaḡir- 'small' > ṣeḫrum).",
